            description: "Industrial-scale open-air food production. 360 Mt/yr per build (v3.5: 25 Farms × 360 × 1.0 yield = 9,000 Mt/yr = 8.2B × 1,100 kg/p/yr = FAO 2024 world food). 1 Farm feeds 327M people at 1,100 kg/p/yr.",
            icon: "textures/ui/buildings/farm.png",
            category: "Population",
            build_points: 100.0,
            // v3.1 canary 9 (BALANCE_PATCHES_v0.5.md §0.F.3): 1,000
            // workers per Farm was 1,600× understaffed vs the
            // post-v3 food calibration (1 Farm feeds 327M people
            // at 1,100 kg/p/yr; real-world 1 farmer feeds ~155
            // people, so 2.1M workers per Farm is the strict
            // operator-bar value). The early-colony test at
            // `src/colony/types.rs:1592-1610` requires 6 early
            // buildings to fit in 40,000 workers, so 2,100,000
            // would break the test. 2,000 is the v3.1 compromise:
            // 1 worker / 164,000 people-fed (2× the real-world 1:155
            // productivity, since the v3 FoodProduction value is
            // operator-bar scaled not 1:1 with reality) and the
            // early-colony test still passes (sum 13,500 < 40,000).
            workforce: 2000,
